🟢 LayeredControlNFT-v1: The Custom NFT Standard for Layered, Interactive, and Composable NFTs
By Jodel Chad, ChainES Labs

What is LayeredControlNFT-v1?
LayeredControlNFT-v1 is a next-generation NFT metadata standard for a new era of digital collectibles. It allows NFTs to combine 3D models, video, audio, images, and more into a single, interactive, and modular asset. This standard unlocks the true potential of NFTs as creative, programmable, and composable digital objects—far beyond simple images or animations.

Key features include:

Multi-layer support: Bundle as many media types (GLB, video, audio, image) as you like, each as its own layer.

Full interactivity: Move, rotate, drag, or interact with any NFT layer—in browser, dApp, or AR/VR.

Explicit stacking and control: Set the order, position, and behavior of each layer.

Wide compatibility: Works with OpenSea, Metaplex, Solana, Ethereum, and all major wallets.

Why Did We Create LayeredControlNFT-v1?
Breaking Through Old Limits
Legacy NFT standards like ERC-721 and ERC-1155 were built for static digital art and collectibles. But as the NFT space evolves, creators and users want more interactivity, richer media, and composability:

AR/VR worlds and gaming

Multi-modal art (3D, video, audio, overlays)

Programmable NFTs with live rewards and updatable states

We found these experiences impossible with old standards. LayeredControlNFT-v1 is our solution.

A Tool for Creators, Developers, and Collectors
Artists can build interactive, layered NFTs with 3D, animation, and sound in a single token.

Developers can power next-gen dApps, galleries, and metaverses using composable NFT building blocks.

Collectors get true digital ownership—NFTs that are dynamic, upgradable, and interactive.

Open, Flexible, and Ready for the Future
Open: Free for anyone to use, extend, or implement.

Flexible: Works on any chain, with any media, backward-compatible with all markets.

Extensible: Add new features or types as technology evolves.

Pragmatic: Even if advanced fields aren’t supported, wallets still display your NFT’s main image or animation.

🚀 Core Features
Multi-Layered NFTs:
Any number of 3D models, videos, images, and audio, each as a stackable layer.

Explicit Layer Control:
Set type, stacking order (z_index), position, and per-layer interactivity.

Composable & Extensible:
Add new layer types or controls as technology evolves—no breaking changes.

Interoperable:
Standard fields ensure all wallets and marketplaces can display your NFT, while advanced fields power next-gen features.

